      ],
      "extract": "Chiral low-energy constants (LECs) are the coupling constants of effective chiral Lagrangians. They are independent of the light quark masses by construction and they describe the influence of all ``heavy'' degrees of freedom that are not contained explicitly in the effective Lagrangians. The construction of effective Lagrangians is based on symmetry considerations only so that a lot of information is lost in going",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-001-strong-interactions",
