        {
          "term": "cite buettiker",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "At lowest order in the chiral expansion, there are only two LECs $B$ and $F$. $B$ depends on the QCD renormalization scale and always appears multiplied by quark masses in CHPT amplitudes. The products $B m_q$ and the constant $F$ can be expressed in terms of meson masses and of the pion decay constant $F_\\pi$. Those relations involve LECs of $O(p^4)$ or higher to be discussed subsequently. The strong chiral",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
